Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: qcom-nvmem: use dev_err_probe() for OPP config failure

On MSM8953 the CPU nodes carry interconnect paths to the BIMC and to the
APCS CCI clock controller (b011050.clock-controller). When
qcom-cpufreq-nvmem probes before both interconnect providers have
registered, dev_pm_opp_set_config() fails in _allocate_opp_table() ->
dev_pm_opp_of_find_icc_paths() with -EPROBE_DEFER (the table is created
with getclk = false, so no clock or regulator lookup is involved and the
interconnect lookup is the only path that can defer). The driver logs that as an error:

  cpu cpu0: Failed to set OPP config
  cpu cpu0: Failed to set OPP config

and then probes successfully on a later pass, so cpufreq works but the
boot log carries two errors that look like a real failure.

Use dev_err_probe() on the platform device, so a deferral is silent
(and recorded in /sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred with its reason)
while any other error is still printed, now with its error code.

---
diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-nvmem.c b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-nvmem.c
index d706a7677..e0b4a1cbc 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-nvmem.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-nvmem.c
@@ -560,8 +560,10 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		if (config.supported_hw) {
 			drv->cpus[cpu].opp_token = dev_pm_opp_set_config(cpu_dev, &config);
 			if (drv->cpus[cpu].opp_token < 0) {
-				ret = drv->cpus[cpu].opp_token;
-				dev_err(cpu_dev, "Failed to set OPP config\n");
+				ret = dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev,
+						    drv->cpus[cpu].opp_token,
+						    "%s: failed to set OPP config\n",
+						    dev_name(cpu_dev));
 				goto free_opp;
 			}
 		}
